rounded_ties.plain, line 2: Add brackets, or reword this, so it has only one meaning.

    show the total of a list of 1.25 and 2.5 rounded
    ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
Try one of these:
    show the total of a list of 1.25 and (2.5 rounded)
  or
    show (the total of a list of 1.25 and 2.5) rounded
Why: This line can mean two things. Plain never guesses, so you choose.

rounded_ties.plain, line 3: Add brackets to show that "rounded" goes with everything before it.

    show the total of amounts where (it is more than 100) rounded
         ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
Try this:
    show (the total of amounts where it is more than 100) rounded
Why: "rounded" goes after a value, and here it would go with the check in brackets, which is yes or no.

